From 32fdbc9c9762d8363e22d5494e4537523e76c30b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AuraLite <auralite@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 17:07:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] UPKEEP U7: GUI and monitor get capability authentication
 (plan complete)

The launcher API, its /ws proxy and the direct --monitor endpoint were
unauthenticated: any web page (cross-origin or DNS-rebinding), any
local process, and any network peer on an explicit remote bind had
full run control. Measured against RFC 6455 4.2.2/10.1/10.2 (Origin is
unforgeable only by browsers, so it can never be the whole answer):

- Launcher: Host allowlist on every route (403), same-origin Origin
  for mutations and /ws (403), and a capability token for the API and
  the splice (401; X-X86emu-Token / Bearer / ?token= / SameSite=Strict
  HttpOnly cookie). Loopback embeds a per-process token in the served
  page, so the one-click flow is unchanged; a remote bind serves a
  login form and uses the persistent 0600 access-token file the
  desktop GUI shows and rotates (expert mode, network tab), with the
  plaintext warning printed at startup. Each machine run gets its own
  monitor token through the child environment, never argv (absent
  from ps and argv.json), presented by the proxy and the desktop GUI.
- Monitor: --monitor-token= or X86EMU_MONITOR_TOKEN; Host allowlist
  and same-origin Origin on the upgrade; the token gates the upgrade
  (constant-work compare); a non-loopback bind with no token is
  refused before any socket exists, with the plaintext warning when
  it does bind. Tokenless loopback keeps its shape apart from the
  Host/Origin checks, so all 55 pre-U7 wire checks pass untouched.
- tools/gui_app.py: fixes a latent missing `import subprocess`.

Vectors: test_monitor lane auth (16), test_gui_launcher lane E
(13 loopback + 9 remote; happy paths scrape the page token exactly
like a browser), test_gui_app lane C (tokenless client refused;
token absent from argv.json). NC against 41a850e: monitor 10/16 FAIL
(positive carriers pass there because the old code upgrades anyone),
launcher 22 U7 FAILs, gui_app exactly the refusal check. Gates:
make test and make test-sanitize green with both live SeaBIOS ISO
lanes; test-gui/test-monitor/test-monitor-codec green. Closes
UPKEEP_PLAN (D1-D7) and ROADMAP row 4; the gdbstub's loopback
protocol stance is recorded, not changed.
